      "content": "# Test Checklist\n\n## Functionality\n- [ ] FT-1: Users can create financial records by writing text input fields.\n\n- [ ] FT-2: Users can view the financial dashboard.\n\n- [ ] FT-3: Users can search for financial information by entering keywords.\n\n- [ ] FT-4: Users can view and print basic financial summary tables.\n\n- [ ] FT-5: Users can filter the product list by product category (such as expenditure, date, transaction).\n\n- [ ] FT-6: Users can create new financial records.\n\n- [ ] FT-7: Users can manage the financial records they have created.\n\n- [ ] FT-8: Users can customize account categories or accounts.\n\n- [ ] FT-9: Users can categorize the financial records they create.\n\n- [ ] FT-10: Users can view and adjust various items.\n\n- [ ] FT-11: Users can mark projects as tax-related.\n\n## Constraint\n- [ ] CS-12: After a user applies filtering or sorting criteria, the product results displayed by the system must strictly match the selected criteria.\n\n- [ ] CS-13: Users cannot create financial records without any input.\n\n- [ ] CS-14: When adding a new financial record, the selected time period cannot be a future time.\n\n- [ ] CS-15: The start time of the filtering dates must be earlier than the end time.\n\n## Interaction\n- [ ] IX-16: Dashboard information changes in real time when financial information is added, edited, or deleted.\n\n- [ ] IX-17: When a user marks a project as tax-related, the corresponding page should provide feedback.\n\n- [ ] IX-18: When users create and manage financial records, custom accounts show the already assigned records.\n\n- [ ] IX-19: Click \"Print Report,\" and the printed report will appear in the document selection menu.\n\n## Content\n- [ ] CT-20: Users can view their spending and expenditure details.\n\n- [ ] CT-21: The information on the financial dashboard must match the actual financial information entered."
    }
  }
}
